      "writtenOn": "2026-02-16T16:03:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tried wiring the `oauth` plugin to use `@external_deps` in in-tree build mode.\n\nThe in-tree build fails because `external_deps` doesn’t define plugin-only artifacts that are not shipped in release.war (e.g. `com.sap.cloud.security:java-security`).\n\nFor example:\n\n```\nno such target \u0027@…external_deps//:com_sap_cloud_security_env\u0027\n```\n\nTo make this work we’d have to add those plugin-specific deps to Gerrit core’s deps/lockfile so the labels exist, which doesn’t scale across gerrit plugins (this was feasible for Gerrit — JGit integration, though).\n\nSo plugin deps need to remain in a separate `maven_install`. The overlap/allowlist checks in `bazlets` are intended to prevent plugins from bundling libraries already provided by Gerrit and avoid version skew at runtime.\n\nWhat I’m already testing with two new `bazlets` checks (see the end of this series):\n\n* `runtime_jars_allowlist_test`: ensures that no new runtime dependencies are added unnoticed\n* `oauth_no_overlap_with_gerrit`: fails if the plugin bundles artifacts already present in Gerrit’s release.war.jars.txt",
      "parentUuid": "90d5cae3_83c588d8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 141,
