      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The existing overlap/allowlist checks in bazlets (e.g. runtime_jars_allowlist_test and \u003cplugin\u003e_no_overlap_with_gerrit) still ensure that plugins do not accidentally bundle libraries already provided by Gerrit’s runtime, so this approach should remain safe from version skew at runtime.\n\nThis only works for in-tree builds, but not if the plugin is built standalone. Of course our CI currently only performs in-tree builds, but for some users with unofficial plugins this might lead to unwanted results. We should at least document that.",
